.th MACRO I 2/11/76
.sh NAME
macro \*- macro assembler
.sh SYNOPSIS
.bd macro
[option ...] file1 file2 ... filen
.sh DESCRIPTION
.it Macro
assembles the concatenation of the specified files terminating
when a ".end" directive is encountered.
The resulting object file is usually named "filen.obj" (see below).
If a file argument does not contain a dot, then "file.mac"
will be sought as an alternative
.bd before
"file" itself.
.s3
Options, if desired,
may appear anywhere in the command,
and may be chosen from the following list:
.s3
.ft I
.lp +10 9
option	meaning
.ft R
.s3
.lp +10 9
-ls	produce an assembly listing file named "filen.lst"
.s3
.lp +10 9
-cr	produce a cross-reference listing file named "filen.lst".
if the "-ls" option is also included,
the cross-reference listing is appended to the assembly listing.
.s3
.lp +10 9
-lp	the same as "-ls" but causes "filen.lst" to be spooled
for printing.
The listing file is removed after printing.
.s3
.lp +10 9
-no	no object file is produced.
This is useful for syntax checking or producing listings alone.
.s3
.lp +10 9
-ns	all symbol information is left out of the resultant object files.
.s3
.lp +10 9
-li
.lp +10 9
-nl	allow entry of ".list" and ".nlist" directives on the command
line as below:

		macro "-li:meb,com"
.s3
.lp +10 9
-en
.lp +10 9
-ds	allows the entry of ".enabl" and ".dsabl" directives
in a similar way to directives used with
"-li" and "-nl".
.s3
.lp +10 9
-na:file	specifies the output file name(s).
All output files which would normally be of the type "filen.xxx"
become "file.xxx".
.s3
.lp +10 9
-ls:\fIn\fR	allocates an extra \fIn\fRK words of space for the
symbol table and macro storage.
.i0
.dt
.s3
Certain installations have included ``,'' as well as `` ''
as a shell argument separator
and so commas in the "-li", "-nl", "-en" and "-ds" options
must be escaped.
.sh FILES
.nf
.if t .ta 1.2i
.if n .ta 20
/lib/sysmac.sml	system macro library
/bin/macxrf	cross-reference post-processor
/bin/lpr	print spooler
filen.xrf	intermediate cross-reference temporary file
.fi
.sh "SEE ALSO"
DEC macro-11 manual
.br
macro (VII)
.sh BUGS
.it
Macro may loop when short of memory.
See "-xs" and "-ls:\fIn\fR".
